Package: oneplus-erhai-ptyxis
Version: 0.3
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: ptyxis (>= 50), libvte-2.91-gtk4-0
Description: Touch-friendly Ptyxis (GNOME terminal) for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 A patched build of Ptyxis with touchscreen features:
  * one-finger drag scrolls the terminal contents (1:1 with the finger for
    slow movement, accelerated up to 1.3x for fast swipes, and gliding to a
    stop after release); dragging a selection handle or the marked end near
    the top/bottom edge auto-scrolls, faster the closer it gets to the edge;
  * a long press marks text: the word under the finger is selected, dragging
    extends it, and on release the marked region is colour-inverted, copied
    to the clipboard with a "Copied to clipboard" toast, and two draggable
    handles appear to adjust the region (releasing a handle re-copies); the
    marking goes away as soon as you send input to the terminal (typing, the
    on-screen keyboard, a paste) or tap outside it, exactly like a text
    selection;
  * a plain tap is forwarded to the application as a left mouse click when it
    wants mouse events (micro, vim, less, ...), so tapping moves its text
    cursor to the tapped cell exactly as in unpatched Ptyxis;
  * a Paste button in the header bar, right of the new-tab button, so pasting
    is one tap away on a touchscreen (it follows the active tab's clipboard
    state and is insensitive while there is nothing pastable).
 .
 Ptyxis is a C/GTK4/VTE application, so this is a source patch (of
 src/ptyxis-terminal.c, src/ptyxis-window.c and src/ptyxis-window.ui), not an
 extension.  The package installs the patched
 /usr/bin/ptyxis by diverting Ubuntu's binary (kept as /usr/bin/ptyxis.erhai-orig);
 removing the package restores it.  Mouse and keyboard behaviour is unchanged.
 .
 Already-running Ptyxis windows keep the old binary (the app is
 single-instance), so close all Ptyxis windows once after installing to pick
 up the new one.
 Package README: /usr/share/oneplus-erhai-ptyxis/README.md
 Source patch:   /usr/share/oneplus-erhai-ptyxis/ptyxis-erhai-touch.patch
